<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="csrf-token" content="${pdict.csrf.token}">

    <isif condition="${pdict.meta}">
        <isloop items="${pdict.meta}" var="metaTag">
            <isprint value="${metaTag}" encoding="off" />
        </isloop>
    </isif>

    <isinclude url="${URLUtils.url('Inertia-Head', 'component', pdict.page.component)}" />
</head>

<body>
    <!--
    THESIS: A storefront as a fashion-house lookbook — type at architectural
    scale IS the interface; refuses the card-grid, soft-shadow commerce default.
    OWN-WORLD: Strict black & white, zero radius, no shadows; expanded-caps
    Archivo display (wdth 125), tracked label caps for nav/CTAs, mono only for
    data (counts, SKUs, prices, code); hairline rules; depth by inversion only.
    STORY: A visitor is stopped by a viewport-filling headline, walks a
    lookbook of bare imagery into a collection, and buys without chrome.
    FIRST VIEWPORT: "TIME, / WELL CHOSEN." stacked at ~9rem expanded caps
    over a hairline grid; label-caps CTA pair; UI copy is English.
    FORM: User-pinned world (high-fashion design agency) — beats the roll.
    FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the
    finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
    -->
    <iscomment>
        The @inertiajs v3.6 client boots from this JSON script tag
        (script[data-page="app"][type="application/json"]) and mounts into the
        empty #app div. pageJson is pre-escaped by the adapter (angle brackets are JSON-escaped so a prop value can never break out of this script tag).
    </iscomment>
    <script data-page="app" type="application/json"><isprint value="${pdict.pageJson}" encoding="off"/></script>
    <div id="app"></div>
</body>

</html>
